		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=862#p862"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I would love to get a sense of where some of the proprietary physics engines are going with collision detection and contact handling. </div></blockquote>Proprietary physics engines go pretty much the same direction as Bullet Physics. Just use convex (GJK or SAT or other) instead of moving concave. Bullet will get SAT next to GJK, more as a performance comparison. Postings on the ODE forum indicate that moving trimesh doesn't work very well.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Apr 05, 2006 6:40 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
